lowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the batch allowance of 1000 requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header with a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states the refusal carries a Retry-After header.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header with a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text specifies the header value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the refusal body is JSON.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in, the cap, and the tier as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the body names the window, cap, and tier.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in, the cap, and the tier as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly names both the cap and tier in the body.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states this point about the gateway's superior information.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the gateway does the same arithmetic on the 503 path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A 200 wants nothing\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim about the 200 response.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states what a 429 response wants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states this claim about 500 responses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly identifies 503 as the overload path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The four cases are not interchangeable.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states this claim about retry behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states batch is 1000, which is 10 times the default of 100, not 50 times.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window, measured over exactly the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states batch credentials are measured over exactly the same window.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states when the tier is set.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and cannot be asked for per call.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states the tier cannot be requested per call.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this about the tiers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons: a credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text lists three reasons that exclude rate limits; rate limits are a separate reason discussed earlier, making four reasons total, not three with one being the cap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-030\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a credential may be suspended\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states this as one refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-031\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly lists this as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-032\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly lists this as a refusal reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-033\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this about the three reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-034\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states this consequence of retrying against a suspended credential.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-035\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states what the log shows in this scenario.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-036\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this about separating the cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-037\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it costs one comparison.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states that reading the status code costs one comparison.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-038\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-039\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"but the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is zero.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states that zero caps are raised without measurement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-040\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\",\n      \"evidence_source\": 