on the cap is there at all.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Retrying immediately is retrying at once; largest single reason equals most of the reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text names the header as Retry-After.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header with a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text specifies the header value is a whole number of seconds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header with a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the header is present on refusals due to rate limits but does not confirm it on all other refusals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states that waiting longer than the header specifies earns no benefit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states the body is JSON.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in, the cap, and the tier as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states these fields are named but does not specify they are plain fields or how they are presented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states there are four rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the rules should be applied in the order they are given.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this about the gateway's computation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"with information the caller does not have\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the gateway used information the caller cannot access.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states the same arithmetic rule applies to the 503 path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text identifies 503 as the overload path but does not explicitly state the causes differ entirely.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Retry only what is safe to retry.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states that only safe requests should be retried.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Retry only what is safe to retry. A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Safe-to-retry responses are specified; not all non-success responses appear in this list.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A 200 wants nothing\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states that a 200 response wants no action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states what a 429 requires.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states when a 500 can be retried.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and a 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text identifies the 503 response as indicating platform overload.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states the batch allowance of 1000 requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states batch is 1000, which is 10 times the default of 100, not 50 times.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window, measured over exactly the same window.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states batch uses exactly the same window, so it is not a separate counting scheme.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-030\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states nothing else differs, which entails the window, header, and body are identical.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-031\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"If nothing differs between tiers, a client needs no changes to work with either tier.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-032\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this about the tiers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-033\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Log every refusal seen.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states that every refusal should be logged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-034\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text implies logs should be kept a week but does not explicitly state a minimum retention period.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-035\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states that inability to report refusals prevents arguing for increased capacity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-036\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the platform team will not make a case for the caller.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-037\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states there are three reasons for refusals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-038\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons: a credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The three listed reasons exclude rate limits; none of them are rate limit caps, contradicting the claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-039\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons: a credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"All three reasons have nothing to do with traffic volume in the window, not just two.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-040\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a credential may be suspended\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text explicitly states credentials can be suspended.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-041\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states routes can be closed for maintenance, which includes repair.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-042\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states body size limits but does not specify when the refusal occurs in the processing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-043\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Spending whole budget without reaching service is equivalent to burning budget and reaching nothing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-044\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text shows a long run of refusals and no other activity, meaning no successes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-045\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text does not explicitly state that the wasted budget belongs to the caller themselves.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-046\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Getting what it needs without cap change means not needing a larger cap in the first place.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-047\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text does not state whether load shifting is available to almost everybody.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-048\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cap can be raised\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-049\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text states the team looks at load pattern but does not explicitly state this occurs before examining the number.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-050\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text directly states the channel for requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-051\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There is no expedited path\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-052\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and they are answered within two working days.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text specifies the response timeframe as two working days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-053\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The text does not state whether following up affects the response timeline.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":130156,"type":"result","duration_ms":199826,"uuid":"c55d3592-0af7-4ab2-a9cd-b6d74631bac8","ttft_stream_ms":1131,"time_to_request_ms":90,"first_content_frame_ms":1131,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
